+Throws if the text cannot be parsed, and the message says which kind of failure
+it was. Text the grammar never recognises throws `Invalid rule text: cannot parse ...`, which covers `'gibberish nonsense'` and the empty string. Text that
+starts parsing and then fails keeps the grammar's own message: `'every'` and
+`'every 0 days'` throw `Unexpected end`, and `'every 2 fortnights'` throws
+`Unknown symbol`.
