+The date after `until` is handed to the host's `Date.parse`, which has two
+consequences worth knowing before passing user input to it. The month comes
+first in the numeric forms, so `'every day until 3/4/2020'` means March 4 and
+`'every day until 25/12/2020'` throws. And a date with no year is not the
+current year: `Date.parse` supplies 2001, so `'every day until January 1'`
+produces a rule that expired long ago. Always give a year, and prefer a month
+name or the `2020-03-04` form for input you do not control.
